# 2. GENERAL STELLAR WALLET INTEROPERABILITY

## 2.1 Replace the Freighter-centric external wallet experience

TrustFlow must not present external wallet linking as a Freighter-only feature.

The desired user experience is:

1. User opens Profile or the wallet connection area.
2. User clicks one general-purpose "Connect Stellar Wallet" button.
3. TrustFlow presents a wallet-selection interface.
4. User chooses a compatible Stellar wallet.
5. The selected wallet requests connection approval.
6. TrustFlow retrieves the selected public Stellar address.
7. TrustFlow presents an explicit ownership-verification message.
8. User signs the message inside the selected wallet.
9. TrustFlow sends the challenge and signature to the backend.
10. Backend verifies the signature and challenge.
11. Only after successful verification is the external wallet linked to the authenticated TrustFlow user.

The user must be able to cancel the connection or signing request without creating a partially verified wallet record.

The UI should communicate the selected wallet and address clearly.

Do not make the user choose Freighter by default or assume that Freighter is installed.

